  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-02-25T18:01:29.924Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I use HTC Vive Pro with FBT.\n\nSituation:\nYou talk or cuddle with someone and play with your ears and face expression (trigger value). Boom! Suddenly you are in a chair at the other end of the room. Or a pillow sticks on your hands, which was 10meters away from you. This breaks immersion immediatelly and this is not what FBT users want.\n\nThe grab range of objects is set by the world creators (they doesn't limit this always to reasonable values). Especially with Vive, there is no possibility to configure the trigger value, at which point an object will be grabed. There are a setting in the Steam VR Controller. But set Grab/Interact to a trigger value of 1, let you loss the ability to use GestureRightWeight/GestureLeftWeight in your animation controller. Face expressions or wiggling ears/tails are gone then.\n\nMy girlfriend has an Valve Index. Apparently there are extended options in Steam VR for it. So, there seems to be separate configurations for Grab and Interact.\n\nChange Request:\n- Let us configure, at which trigger value things will be grabed, whitout GestureLeftWeight/GestureRightWeight are affected in the animation controller. This specially for Vive Controllers.\n\n- Chairs, which will be activated by a button (dance worlds for example) are ok. But let us disable chair trigger colliders, which reacts on your trigger of your controller. This could be done globally in the settings or action menu (\"Disable Chair Colliders\").\n\n- Let us override the grab distance ob interactable objects with a new setting in the action menu (\"Disable Interaction\"). It should be uncomplicated to toggle this setting depending of the current world. Additional, the range should be be configurable, when interaction override is active (\"Override Grab Range\" from 10cm to 2m for example).",
